  "text": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "I am Mia. It is dinner time. We eat at the table. Mom has rice. The rice is good. Dad has a burger. \"Look, Mia,\" says Dad. \"Burger is a Thai word too.\" I smile.",
      "The TV is on. \"Hockey!\" says Dad. The men jump. I look at the ball. The ball is white. \"Hockey is a Thai word too,\" says Mom. \"Football is a Thai word,\" I say. \"Is jump a Thai word?\" asks Dad. \"No,\" I say. We smile.",
      "Then we have ice cream. Mom has coconut ice cream. I have chocolate. It is good. \"Ice cream is a Thai word!\" says Mom. \"Chocolate is a Thai word!\" I say. I jump. We know many English words. \"Yes, we do!\" says Dad."
    ],
    "summary": "Mia has dinner with Mom and Dad. They find English words that Thai people say too, like burger, hockey, and chocolate.",
